                },
                {
                  "id": "intro-text",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "prose",
                    "text": "Electrical problems have become one of the most common reasons modern commercial trucks end up in the service bay. With today’s heavy-duty vehicles relying on dozens of sensors, electronic control modules, wiring harnesses, and onboard computers, even a small electrical issue can quickly turn into unexpected downtime. That’s why professional electrical diagnostic tools have become essential for keeping trucks on the road. Rather than guessing what’s wrong or replacing parts unnecessarily, experienced technicians can pinpoint the source of a problem before it turns into a costly breakdown."
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-2",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Why Electrical Systems Matter More Than Ever"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Commercial trucks today are more advanced than ever before. Electrical systems control critical components like:"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-systems",
          "type": "list",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "label": "Engine management"
              },
              {
                "label": "Transmission operation"
              },
              {
                "label": "Anti-lock braking systems (ABS)"
              },
              {
                "label": "Emissions equipment"
              },
              {
                "label": "Battery charging systems"
              },
              {
                "label": "Lighting"
              },
              {
                "label": "Safety features"
              },
              {
                "label": "Driver information displays"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-b",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "When one sensor or circuit begins to fail, it can create a chain reaction of warning lights, performance issues, and unexpected shutdowns."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-3",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading-2",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "How Electrical Diagnostic Tools Find Problems Faster"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-2",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Modern electrical diagnostic tools do much more than read fault codes. Professional diagnostic equipment communicates directly with the truck’s onboard computer systems, allowing technicians to monitor real-time performance and isolate electrical faults that aren’t always visible during a physical inspection.\n\nThese tools help identify issues involving:"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-2-faults",
          "type": "list",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "label": "Wiring failures"
              },
              {
                "label": "Faulty sensors"
              },
              {
                "label": "Battery and charging systems"
              },
              {
                "label": "Alternator performance"
              },
              {
                "label": "Electronic control modules (ECMs)"
              },
              {
                "label": "Communication network failures"
              },
              {
                "label": "Switches and relays"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-2-b",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Instead of replacing multiple components through trial and error, technicians can focus on repairing the actual source of the problem. That means less downtime, fewer unnecessary repairs, and lower operating costs."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-4",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "image-2",
          "type": "image",
          "props": {
            "width": "prose",
            "image": {
              "src": "https://vendure.buzznerdrv.com/assets/source/db/2.2.jpg",
              "alt": "2.2.jpg",
              "width": 1150,
              "height": 1000
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-5",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading-3",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Common Signs You Need Truck Electrical Diagnostics"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Electrical problems don’t always announce themselves with a complete failure. Watch for these warning signs:"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-warn-h",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Dashboard Warning Lights"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-warn-p",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Check engine lights, ABS warnings, battery indicators, or transmission alerts should never be ignored."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-start-h",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Hard Starting"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-start-p",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "If your truck struggles to start consistently, the issue may involve batteries, cables, sensors, or the charging system."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-lights-h",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Flickering or Dim Lights"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-lights-p",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Lighting problems often point to voltage issues, alternator concerns, or deteriorating wiring."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-inter-h",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Intermittent Performance Problems"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-inter-p",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Random shutdowns, loss of power, or electronic glitches frequently require professional truck electrical diagnostics to accurately diagnose."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-3-b",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "The earlier these issues are addressed, the less likely they are to become expensive roadside repairs."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-6",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading-4",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Electrical Issues Can Affect More Than Electronics"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-4",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "One of the biggest misconceptions is that electrical failures only affect electronics. In reality, faulty sensors can impact:"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-4-impact",
          "type": "list",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "label": "Fuel efficiency"
              },
              {
                "label": "Engine performance"
              },
              {
                "label": "Emissions systems"
              },
              {
                "label": "Transmission shifting"
              },
              {
                "label": "Cooling systems"
              },
              {
                "label": "Driver safety features"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-4-b",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Because so many systems communicate electronically, one damaged connector or failing module can create symptoms that appear mechanical when they’re actually electrical. That’s why experienced technicians rely on diagnostics before recommending repairs."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-7",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading-5",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Why Professional Diagnostics Beat Guesswork"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-5",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "There are countless code readers and aftermarket electrical diagnostic tools available today, but reading a fault code is only one piece of the puzzle. A diagnostic code tells technicians where the computer detected a problem, not necessarily what caused it.\n\nFor example, a sensor code may actually be caused by:"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-5-causes",
          "type": "list",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "label": "Damaged wiring"
              },
              {
                "label": "Poor grounding"
              },
              {
                "label": "Low battery voltage"
              },
              {
                "label": "Connector corrosion"
              },
              {
                "label": "A failed control module"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-5-b",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Professional technicians combine advanced diagnostic equipment with years of experience to determine the root cause instead of replacing parts unnecessarily. That’s why working with an experienced diesel mechanic for semi trucks often saves both time and money."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-8",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading-6",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Quality Parts Make Repairs Last"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-6",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Once technicians identify the issue, using dependable replacement components is just as important as making the correct diagnosis. Whether you need sensors, switches, relays, batteries, wiring components, or other electrical parts, the Sun State International Online Parts Store provides access to quality parts designed for commercial trucks. Installing reliable components helps reduce repeat failures and keeps your electrical system operating the way it was designed."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-9",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "heading-7",
          "type": "heading",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 2,
            "align": "left",
            "text": "Preventive Diagnostics Should Be Part of Semi Truck Maintenance"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-7",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "Many electrical failures develop gradually over time. Including routine inspections and truck electrical diagnostics as part of your regular semi truck maintenance schedule allows technicians to catch problems before they result in expensive roadside breakdowns.\n\nPreventive diagnostics are especially valuable for:"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-7-for",
          "type": "list",
          "props": {
            "headingLevel": 3,
            "columns": 2,
            "items": [
              {
                "label": "Fleet vehicles"
              },
              {
                "label": "High-mileage trucks"
              },
              {
                "label": "Long-haul operations"
              },
              {
                "label": "Trucks operating in harsh weather"
              },
              {
                "label": "Vehicles with recurring warning lights"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "text-7-b",
          "type": "text",
          "props": {
            "align": "left",
            "width": "prose",
            "text": "A proactive maintenance strategy helps maximize uptime while reducing emergency repair costs."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "spacer-10",
          "type": "spacer",
          "props": {
            "size": 6
          }
        },
        {
